IMPORT prelude

-- Building Maintenance and Strata Management Act 2004 (Singapore) -- the owner's (subsidiary proprietor's) position: renovating the
-- lot (ss 37, 37A), contributions and arrears (ss 39 to 41), the statutory charge and power of sale (s 43), the guarantee of the
-- management corporation's debts (s 44), council eligibility and removal for arrears (ss 53, 54), and neighbourly duties (s 63).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BSMA2004.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 15 of 2026 shown (some in force 1 July and 1 October 2026; s 38(3)(d), (e) not yet in operation). The deposit's
-- arrangement of sections runs out of step with the body; the encoding follows the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 17 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository; pairs with the Land Titles (Strata) Act row
-- (collective sale). SCOPED to what an owner faces. Not encoded: the schedule of strata units (Part 4), developer management
-- (Part 5 Division 1), meetings, by-laws, insurance, subsidiary management corporations, managing agents, the Strata Titles
-- Boards (Part 6), and the Schedules (including the voting rules).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Building Maintenance and Strata Management Act 2004 -- owners`

§§ `37, 37A -- renovating the lot`

-- s 37(1), (2): an improvement that increases or is likely to increase FLOOR AREA needs a 90% RESOLUTION of the management
-- corporation (and, (2A), planning permission as well). (3), (4): one that affects the APPEARANCE of the building needs the
-- management corporation's authority, given only if it will not detract from the appearance and will not affect structural
-- integrity. (4A): the management corporation may require the CURRENT owner to remedy a contravention at their own cost
-- "whether or not the subsidiary proprietor is responsible for the contravention".
-- s 37A: SAFETY EQUIPMENT -- window grilles, balcony railings, window restrictors, insect and animal screens, intruder alarms,
-- locks -- may be installed "despite ... any by-law ... which otherwise prohibits" it, if installed competently and in keeping
-- with the building's appearance.
DECLARE Renovation IS ONE OF
    `enclosing a balcony to add floor area`
    `changing the facade colour of the windows`
    `installing window grilles`
    `installing a cat-proof mesh`
    `installing a CCTV intruder monitoring system`
    `re-tiling the kitchen`

GIVEN `the renovation` IS A Renovation
GIVETH A STRING
`what the renovation needs` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the renovation`
    WHEN `enclosing a balcony to add floor area` THEN "a 90% resolution"
    WHEN `changing the facade colour of the windows` THEN "management corporation approval"
    WHEN `re-tiling the kitchen` THEN "nothing under section 37"
    OTHERWISE "nothing: section 37A overrides the by-laws"

GIVEN `responsible for the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `is the current owner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner can be required to remedy an unauthorised improvement` IF
    `is the current owner`

§§ `39 to 41 -- contributions`

-- s 40(2): contributions are payable "in shares proportional to the share value" of the lots.
-- s 40(3): a new owner is "jointly and severally liable" with the former owner for contributions unpaid when they became owner.
-- (4): a former owner is liable only for what was unpaid when they ceased to be owner.
-- (6)(b): interest runs from the 30th day after the due date, at the rate the management corporation sets, unless it decides
-- otherwise in general meeting.
-- (9), (10): after a written demand, an owner who has not paid "before the 14th day after the date of service" commits an
-- OFFENCE -- a fine up to $10,000, plus $100 a day after conviction.
-- s 41(1): while the building is under construction, contributions on a proposed lot are reduced by 75%, until the TOP
-- (2).
GIVEN `the budget` IS A NUMBER, `my share value` IS A NUMBER, `aggregate share value` IS A NUMBER, `under construction` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my contribution` MEANS
    IF `under construction`
    THEN `the budget` TIMES `my share value` DIVIDED BY `aggregate share value` TIMES 1 DIVIDED BY 4
    ELSE `the budget` TIMES `my share value` DIVIDED BY `aggregate share value`

DECLARE Liable IS ONE OF
    `the seller only`
    `the buyer only`
    `the seller and the buyer jointly and severally`

GIVEN `arrears arose before the sale` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Liable
`who is liable for the arrears` MEANS
    IF `arrears arose before the sale` THEN `the seller and the buyer jointly and severally` ELSE `the buyer only`

GIVEN `days after the due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `interest is running` IF
    `days after the due date` GREATER THAN 30

GIVEN `demand served` IS A BOOLEAN, `days since the demand` IS A NUMBER, `paid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `non-payment is an offence` IF
    `demand served` AND (NOT `paid`) AND `days since the demand` AT LEAST 14

§§ `43 -- charge and power of sale`

-- s 43(1): contributions unpaid 30 days after a written demand become, on lodgment and registration, a CHARGE on the lot. (2): the
-- management corporation then has a power of SALE as if it were a registered mortgagee -- ranking after public authorities'
-- statutory charges and earlier-registered encumbrances. (3): but it may sell only if (a) a SPECIAL RESOLUTION authorises it,
-- (b) notice has been published in a daily newspaper, (c) nothing is paid within 6 WEEKS after publication, and (d) no court
-- action to restrain the sale is pending.
DECLARE Arrears HAS
    `days since demand` IS A NUMBER
    `charge registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `special resolution passed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `newspaper notice published` IS A BOOLEAN
    `weeks since publication` IS A NUMBER
    `paid after publication` IS A BOOLEAN
    `restraining action pending` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the arrears` IS AN Arrears
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a charge may be registered` IF
    `the arrears`'s `days since demand` GREATER THAN 30

GIVEN `the arrears` IS AN Arrears
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the management corporation may sell the flat` IF
        `the arrears`'s `charge registered`
    AND `the arrears`'s `special resolution passed`
    AND `the arrears`'s `newspaper notice published`
    AND `the arrears`'s `weeks since publication` AT LEAST 6
    AND (NOT `the arrears`'s `paid after publication`)
    AND (NOT `the arrears`'s `restraining action pending`)

§§ `44 -- owners guarantee the management corporation's debts`

-- s 44(1): expenditure lawfully incurred by the management corporation "is ... guaranteed by the persons who ... comprise the
-- management corporation" -- the owners. (2): each owner's liability is limited to what they would pay if a contribution were
-- levied to raise the sum.
GIVEN `the debt` IS A NUMBER, `my share value` IS A NUMBER, `aggregate share value` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`my guarantee liability` MEANS
    `the debt` TIMES `my share value` DIVIDED BY `aggregate share value`

§§ `53, 54 -- council and arrears`

-- s 53(7): a candidate is ineligible for the council if, "on the 3rd day before the date of election", ANY contribution on their
-- lot (or on the nominating owner's lot) is in arrears.
-- s 54(2)(a): a council member may be removed WITHOUT a general meeting if contributions are in arrears "for more than 3 months".
GIVEN `any arrears 3 days before the election` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is eligible` IF
    NOT `any arrears 3 days before the election`

GIVEN `months in arrears` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the member can be removed without a general meeting` IF
    `months in arrears` GREATER THAN 3

§§ `63 -- neighbourly duties`

-- s 63: an owner, mortgagee in possession, LESSEE OR OCCUPIER must not interfere with support, shelter or services to other lots;
-- use the lot so as to cause "a nuisance or hazard" to another occupier; or use the common property so as to interfere
-- unreasonably with others' use of it or of their lots. The duty binds tenants directly.
DECLARE Person IS ONE OF
    `owner`
    `tenant`
    `mortgagee in possession`
    `visitor`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 63 binds the person` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`
    WHEN `visitor` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
